# CODEOWNERS — review gates for the surfaces that execute on every session.
#
# Why this file exists (October 2026 hardening): Unown's instruction set is
# code the model executes as behavior, but it *reads* like documentation —
# a single merged poison edit to a rule file persists into every future
# session (AutoRedClaw arXiv:2610.27244; Agent Commander; the "Fable to
# Haiku" subagent-config downgrade chain). Instruction files and the
# guard/gate sources therefore get an explicit owner review on every PR,
# on top of branch protection on main (require PR + review + CI green;
# no direct pushes, no force-push, stale approvals dismissed).
#
# The default owner is the repo maintainer. Replace/add team handles as
# the project grows — the review GATE is the point, not the identity.

# ── Default owner: everything not matched below ────────────────────────────
* @kanishka-namdeo

